  "chapter": {
    "number": 43,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(44) For the end, a Psalm for",
          {
            "noteId": 79
          },
          "instruction, for the sons of Core."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O God, we have heard with our ears, our fathers have told us, the work which you wrought in their days, in the days of old.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your hand utterly destroyed the heathen, and you did plant them: you did afflict the nations, and cast them out.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For they inherited not the land by their own sword, and their own arm did not deliver them; but your right hand, and your arm, and the light of your countenance, because you were well pleased in them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You are indeed my King and my God, who command deliverances for Jacob.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In you will we push down our enemies, and in your name will we bring to nothing them that rise up against us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I will not trust in my bow, and my sword shall not save me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you have saved us from them that afflicted us, and have put to shame them that hated us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In God",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 80
          },
          {
            "text": "will we make our boast all the day, and to your name will we give thanks for ever. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But now you have cast off, and put us to shame; and you will not go forth with our hosts.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have turned us back before our enemies; and they that hated us spoiled for themselves.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You made us as sheep for meat; and you scattered us among the nations.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have sold your people without price, and there was no profit by their exchange.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have made us a reproach to our neighbors, a scorn and derision them that are round about us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have made us a proverb among the Gentiles, a shaking of the head among the nations.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All the day my shame is before me, and the confusion of my face has covered me,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "because of the voice of the slanderer and reviler; because of the enemy and avenger.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All these things are come upon us: but we have not forgotten you, neither have we dealt unrighteously in your covenant.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And our heart has not gone back; but you have turned aside our paths from your way.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you have laid us low in a place of affliction, and the shadow of death has covered us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If we have forgotten the name of our God, and if we have spread out our hands to a strange god; shall not God search these things out?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "for he knows the secrets of the heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For, for your sake we are killed all the day long; we are counted as sheep for slaughter.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Awake, therefore sleep you, O Lord? arise, and do not cast us off for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore turn you your face away, and forget our poverty and our affliction?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For our soul has been brought down to the dust; our belly has cleaved to the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Arise, O Lord, help us, and redeem us for your name's sake.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 79,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. understanding.",
